From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:19:04 +0000
Subject: fix(ios): drop scroll events that carry non-finite values

KRScrollView forwarded NaN/Inf offsets, sizes, velocities and touch
points to Kotlin, where they poisoned scroll state. Validate the core
fields in p_generateEventBaseParams and return nil (logged) when any is
non-finite, skip non-finite touch points, and have every _css_scroll*,
drag and willDragEnd callback site ignore a nil payload. The scroll
block keeps its css_scroll nil check for the async dispatch path.

Fork-Patch: ios-scroll-event-finite-guard
Origin: f35eeb87
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

